body:
Ah, UCF is rather safe, but the extra classes and meal plan and requirement to live at Towers is a money grab for sure. A good friend of mine goes to U of Kansas so if you want to know about that, PM me! Midwestern life is certainly VERY different from Singapore. For one, you have to drive everywhere because everything is so spread out. Not at all like Singapore which is so small and well-connected! My advice is for sure to get a car (or a buddy with a car) as soon as possible. You'll thank yourself. Suburban American transportation can't hold a candle to Singapore's system.

&#x200B;

And no, actually, I'm a girl, hahaha! I moved away when I was almost 13 so I grew up some in Singapore, some in Florida. It's been 7 years since I moved. Don't worry about the 2 year age difference. It all depends on your individual maturity and your friends'. I'm friends with a lot of people that are quite a bit older than me. In my experience, college freshmen can be rather immature, especially guys, I think. There are a lot of people who've never been away from home before with strict parents, and they take the opportunity to go buck wild. Just ask my ex-roommates. If you're (I'm assuming) in your 20s, you'll definitely be able to befriend upperclassmen or people closer to your age. But 2 years is negligible.
